            <tr style="height:63.5500pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;background:rgb(255,255,255);">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Dermatology is a&nbsp;subject&nbsp;in which morphological teaching plays an important role. We hope&nbsp;that each student will grasp&nbsp;the basic characteristics and principles&nbsp;of the dermatology and venereology&nbsp;through the study of this course. Through the teacher's informative presentations,&nbsp;the classroom PPT, books and reference materials,&nbsp;our students&nbsp;will&nbsp;have a basic understanding of dermatology and&nbsp;venereology, and&nbsp;will&nbsp;have a preliminary perception of common diseases. This curriculum will provide the student with clinical internship in both outpatient clinic and&nbsp;wards, which will establish&nbsp;a solid foundation for post-undergraduate and possible future further developments in dermatology.&nbsp;Last but no least, we hope our curriculum will inspire our students’ interest in dermatology.</p></font></span><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:12.0000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
